.TH "DOTTY" "1" "Jun 2026" "Auto generated by spf13/cobra" ""

.SH NAME
dotty-profile-new - Create a profile and set this machine up as one of its class.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotty profile new [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a profile by running the init interview for it: a profile directory
with nothing in it is a machine class that configures nothing, so new is
dotty init with the profile name settled in advance. Without --name dotty
prompts for one, then asks init's questions — where the dotfiles repository
lives, which add-ons and coding agents to include, security keys, macOS
defaults — renders profiles/ into the repository, links the home/ tree,
and activates the profile. Nothing is written until the summary is confirmed.

.PP
Every init flag works here too, so a profile can be created unattended. The
name has to be free: an existing profile is re-rendered with dotty init and
switched to with dotty profile activate.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--addons\fP=[]
	optional add-ons: nvim,btop,k9s,lazygit,lsd,tmux,yazi

.PP
\fB--agents\fP=[]
	coding agents: claude-code,codex,opencode,antigravity,grok

.PP
\fB--allowed-serials\fP=[]
	restrict the profile to these security-key serials

.PP
\fB--description\fP=""
	short description of the profile

.PP
\fB--dump-brews\fP[=false]
	seed the Brewfile from the installed packages

.PP
\fB--git-email\fP=""
	git identity email for the private git config

.PP
\fB--git-name\fP=""
	git identity name for the private git config

.PP
\fB--harden\fP[=false]
	confine the coding agents: sandbox, credential-read denies, ask-first permissions

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for new

.PP
\fB--macos-defaults\fP=[]
	macOS defaults groups to apply (see the wizard picklist; empty for none)

.PP
\fB--marketplace\fP[=false]
	add the bitwise skills marketplace to the selected agents

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	name for the new profile

.PP
\fB--on-conflict\fP="backup"
	existing-file resolution: backup, adopt, skip, or fail

.PP
\fB--piv\fP[=false]
	require smart-card (PIV) login system-wide

.PP
\fB--private-repo\fP=""
	encrypted private dotfiles repository path (empty for none)

.PP
\fB--repo\fP=""
	dotfiles repository path (default /dotfiles)

.PP
\fB--repos-dir\fP=""
	directory your repositories live in (default ~/Repos)

.PP
\fB--security-keys\fP[=false]
	this machine class signs with hardware security keys

.PP
\fB--wallpaper\fP=""
	wallpaper image from ~/.local/share/wallpapers

.PP
\fB--worktrees\fP=""
	agent worktree location: a directory name inside each repo (default .worktrees) or an absolute path

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	skip the confirmation summary and reuse stored answers; only unanswered questions are asked


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to operate on (defaults to the active profile)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  dotty profile new
  dotty profile new --name=work --description="work laptop"
  dotty profile new --name=work --addons=tmux --agents=claude-code --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBdotty-profile(1)\fP
